      PD programs such as Jive, ValSpeak and Kraut
    * message areas can be set to have inappropriate language automatically
      filtered out of messages as they are saved.
    * each user has a private mail directory
    * user can keep a carbon copy of private mail sent
    * message reading in forward and reverse direction
    * private mail traffic can be monitored by the sysop


Here are some features of DLG's online file system:

    * up to 9999 file areas are supported
    * each user's access can be tailored individually for each file area
      or defaults can be set for each.
    * smart menu display (context/access sensitive)
    * full file searching of all available areas with wild card support
    * users can easily scan file areas they wish to monitor for new files
    * each file can have up to a 10K description
    * users can add comments to existing file descriptions to aid others
      with their downloading decision
    * choice quick or verbose listing of all files in an area
    * users can kill files that they uploaded if their access permits
    * trash-can-like directory saves deleted files as a backup against
      accidental or unwanted deletions
    * uploader's custom signature is applied to file descriptions
    * archive content viewing supported for Zip, Arc, Lharc, and Zoo
    * protocols are completely configurable to allow the use of
      external file transfer protocols (XPR) and DLG-compatible protocols
    * Xmodem (Checksum/CRC/1K) and Zmodem protocols included
    * files can be uploaded to another user's private directory
    * batch uploads are supported for appropriate protocols
    * partially uploaded or downloaded files can be resumed at a later date
    * files can be 'tagged' for batch download using appropriate protocols
    * partial 'tagged list' and partial 'file' downloads are supported
    * a tagged file list is retained from call to call and is not deleted 
      until the user does so, or downloads the files it contains
    * user can list and edit his tagged file list
    * DLG supports upload/download ratios
    * individual files can be marked as FREE and will not count on ratios
    * privately uploaded files to a user are FREE
    * default protocol can be set, or can be selected at time of download
    * optional auto-log-off after download
    * files can be transferred from area to area, public to private, or 
      private to public
    * file descriptions indicate number of times download
    * files show approximate download time
    * SysOp can upload and download locally from a local session


Here are some of DLG's features for network support:

    * FidoNet
        - Echomail and Netmail areas are fully integrated into the
          message system
        - separate origin lines can be defined for each Echomail area
        - FidoNet private mail is sent to the users' private mail
          directory for assured reception
        - full cost implementation allows charging for Netmail via
          a user account credit system
        - users are informed of incoming Echo/Netmail in real time
          if they are online or via their event log if they are not.
        - support for outgoing file attaches and file requests
        - can accept file requests from other systems
        - a list of requestable "magic" file names can be created with
          optional password protection
        - file areas can be designated as File Requestable
        - crashmail is supported through third-party front-door programs.
        - can zonegate fidonet messages
        - can receive and send/reply to point systems
        - full Nodelist support of the Traplist format
        - temporary closing of message areas allows importing of FidoNet 
          mail without affecting the operation of the BBS
        - Netmail mail can be addressed to online group mailing lists

    * UUCP/UseNet
        - Each user has their own personal UUCP account
        - UUCP mail can be received in a users private directory
        - UUCP mail can be entered by any user with the proper access
        - UUCP messages can be replied to with one easy key-stroke
        - UUCP mail can be sent to online mailing lists
        - UseNet newsgroups can be imported into message areas
        - UUCICO accounts may be set up to allow the system to give a
          UUCP feed to another site


Message and file area support is standard for most bulletin board system
software. DLG adds to that the excitement of PeopleTalk - multi-user real
time conferencing. Here are some features of DLG's PeopleTalk system:

    * users can create rooms at any time
    * minimum baud rate and user level can be set for each room
    * people can view which users are in a room
    * users in conference can send private messages to others in the same
      room unseen by other members of the conference
    * system wide message broadcast upon room creation


DLG has powerful options for SysOp control of the entire system: Here are
some features:

    * full point and click install program will have you up and running
      within minutes

    * 47 different attributes of each user can be edited, including:
        - user level which determines access to auto-access message and 
          file areas, and to menu command selections.
        - daily and session time limits
        - time used today
        - 'K' uploaded/downloaded
        - upload/download ratio
        - netmail credit
        - bulletin write access
        - UUCP write and client privileges

    * multiple user validation templates make validating new users
      fast and easy
    * users can be purged based on number of days since last call
    * message and file areas can be easily created/edited/deleted
    * groups of users can be created for batch private mailing
    * the language/format of the new user questionnaire is configurable
    * message and file areas can be easily renumbered

    * Chat system
        - SysOp can break into chat with a user at any time
        - user can page the SysOp for chat - a requester is popped on the
          workbench screen that indicates who is paging and the SysOp can
          answer or ignore the chat request
        - two colour chat display with full word wrap

    * Configurable log entries
        - internal log entries can be assigned the user level required to
          view them
        - additional custom log entries can be defined
        - a logging utility is provided so that external tasks such as
          online games and network mail events can be monitored.

    * File maintenance section
        - all files from a particular directory can be uploaded at once
        - SysOp can individually enter file descriptions, specify a single
          file description for all files, or take descriptions from filenotes
        - All attributes of a file can be edited

    * Powerful menu configuration
        - any number of menus can be configured
        - menu items can launch batch files, executables, or other menus
        - any program that runs with standard input/output from a CLI
          can be run from a menu
        - menu items are accessible by user level
        - user's only see the menu items they can access
        - SysOp-editable help files can be attached to any menu item

    * Each port (phone line) can be configured separately for things like:
        - modem configuration
        - BBS Name
        - public vs private (only users in a certain group have access)
        - idle timeout delay
        - minimum baud rate
        - initial menu to be used
        - default login command stack
        - forced login command stack (applied before a user's personal
          login command stack)

    * SysOp can easily monitor users who are online
        - can use a custom screen, or the workbench
        - screens for current online users can be open and closed from
          AmigaDos
        - any screen resolution/depth can be used
        - any non-proportional font can be used
        - can have a screen open automatically as each user logs in or have
          them remain closed for more memory/cpu efficiency
        - can configure screens to open only for only designated users

    * A full resource-management system is provided
        - access to serial ports is managed so that term programs and
          network mail software will not interfere with the BBS
        - automated tasks that use the serial port are assured not to 
          conflict
        - access to message and file areas is managed so that conflicts do
          not arise between users and network mail software

    * A powerful event scheduler is provided
        - necessary for a 24hr automated system - especially if networked
          mail is being used
        - events can be scheduled to occur on any combination of minute hour,
          day of week, day of month, month, and year
        - typical uses include scheduling of mail events, renumbering of
          message areas, dynamically regulating access to phone lines

    * Configurable drop-to-DOS shell
        - SysOp has full access to DOS from remote
        - limited access to DOS can be given to users
        - access to DOS commands is configured based on user level


